Currently, updateSearch ignores the regex settings. E.g. in the Shiny App below after a click on the button "search" we get an empty table.

Note: The fix isn't that nice as I simply copied some code from above. You might want to refactor it into a function. As I don't know much Javascript I didn't really want to try it myself.

```
library(shiny)
library(DT)


shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(
    DT::dataTableOutput("tbl"),
    actionButton("but", "search")
  ),
  
  server = function(input, output, session) {
    output$tbl <- DT::renderDataTable(
      data.frame(a = month.name, stringsAsFactors = FALSE),
      options = list(search = list(regex = TRUE)),
      filter = list(position = "bottom")
    )
    
    observeEvent(input$but, {
      DT::updateSearch(DT::dataTableProxy("tbl"), keywords = list(columns = "Jan|Feb"))
    })
  }
)
```

@yihui I tried a few things to see if I could increase the spacing in the column filter boxes. For some reason the padding on the right is currently really high. I removed the form-control class in a few places and, even though the look is not that stylish, the spacing is much improved. With these changes issue #49 also does not occur which is a nice side-effect. I actually like the remove-circle below the box. See the Data > View tab at http://vnijs.rady.ucsd.edu:3838/base (Data > View tab) for the alternative 'look'

I also added an argument to `dataTableAjax` to make it easier to create a custom `dataTablesJSON` function - #66.

Any suggestions on how to make the sliders a bit coarser? It is currently very hard to get to a whole number which is what a user would most likely want, especially for integers.
